  "presentation_summary": [
    "39-year-old man presented with five days of left lower quadrant abdominal pain aggravated by walking.",
    "Symptoms included subjective fever, chills, and decreased stool content; he denied nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and blood in stool.",
    "Vital signs included temperature 36.4 C, heart rate 106, respiratory rate 18, blood pressure 137/80, and oxygen saturation 100% on room air.",
    "Exam showed left lower quadrant tenderness and mild rebound while the abdomen was described as non-peritonitic.",
    "CT abdomen and pelvis showed sigmoid diverticulitis with a small amount of gas and fluid in the surrounding mesocolon consistent with microperforation and no drainable abscess."
  ],
